## Phase 11: Feature Backlog (user-suggested — not yet ordered)
- [x] 80. Recurring tasks — daily/weekly/monthly recurrence with auto-regeneration of the next instance on completion
- [x] 81. Task dependencies — link tasks so a task auto-flips to Blocked while its prerequisite is open, with a visual chain
- [x] 82. Time tracking — per-task timers + manually logged time, totals shown on cards and in reports
- [x] 83. Gantt chart view — project timeline as a real Gantt bar chart (planned vs actual, dependencies drawn as arrows)
- [x] 84. Today / daily planner view — merges due tasks, events, and focus blocks into one time-ordered day timeline
- [x] 85. Portfolio view — cross-project dashboard: all projects' progress bars, burn-down of overdue counts, capacity heat
- [x] 86. File attachments per task/note — drag files in, stored locally via kv (images preview inline, docs downloadable)
- [x] 87. Tag manager — global tag list with colors, rename/merge across all entities, filter-by-tag everywhere
- [x] 88. Recurring backup with versioning — auto-snapshot history (e.g. last 30 days) so you can restore any point in time
- [x] 89. Export to other formats — CSV (tasks/events), Markdown (notes/checklists), and .ics calendar file for Google/Outlook
- [x] 90. Weekly report — auto-generated summary: tasks completed, streaks, focus time, top projects; saveable as a note
- [x] 91. Quick capture — a floating "Add anything" input (global hotkey) that routes by type into tasks/notes/events without switching views
- [ ] 92. Full keyboard navigation — move between views/items with arrow keys, contextual shortcuts, ? help overlay
- [ ] 93. Print / paper-planning mode — print-friendly layouts: weekly planner sheet, daily agenda, checklist pages (CSS @media print)
- [ ] 94. Project templates — pre-built project blueprints (Feature build, Event planning, Move house…) that seed tasks/checklists/milestones
- [ ] 95. Focus analytics — charts of focus sessions per day/week, completion rate of attached tasks, best focus hours
- [ ] 96. Archive & review flow — batch-archive completed tasks, with a review screen to confirm before archiving
- [ ] 97. Smart inbox rules — auto-apply tags/project/priority when creating tasks (e.g. by keyword or due prefix like "today:")
- [ ] 98. PWA / offline install — service worker so the app opens offline and can be "installed" as an app
- [ ] 99. Accessibility & polish pass — WCAG contrast themes, full aria labelling, reduced-motion support
- [ ] 100. Direct import/export via API — expose window.pm.exportJSON()/importJSON() programmatically, plus real endpoints: (a) shareable backup URL via editable-upload plugin (public URL; any tool can GET/PUT the JSON snapshot = genuine REST resource), or (b) socket-RPC sync endpoint via server-plugin so other clients can pull/push snapshots. NOTE: trades the "nothing ever uploaded" local-first rule for convenience — make it a per-user opt-in "Sync" toggle in Settings
- [ ] 101. Full integration into another web-based tool — (a) embeddable iframe mode with deep links (#/project/xyz); (b) .ics export for calendar integration; (c) REST-style sync using the editable-file URL as a shared JSON bus between Project Master and another app; (d) webhooks via server-plugin that push "task changed" payloads to a URL you supply. Full REST isn't natively served by Perchance, so the cleanest fit is the editable-file JSON bus + iframe embed
